      explanation: "EIGRP supports unequal-cost load balancing across feasible successors using the 'variance <multiplier>' command (default 1). Because 6144 / 3072 = 2, setting 'variance 2' allows any feasible successor with a metric ≤ 2 × 3072 (6144) to enter the routing table and share traffic proportionally (B).",
