      correct: "D",
      explanation: "IPv6 compression removes leading zeros in each 16-bit hextet (0db8 → db8, 0700 → 700, 0003 → 3; trailing or interior zeros in 700 and 400F are NEVER removed) and replaces one contiguous run of all-zero hextets (0000:0000) with '::' once only—yielding '2001:db8::700:3:400F:572B/64' (D). Option B illegally uses '::' twice, and A/C illegally drop non-leading zeros.",
