      correct: "D",
      explanation: "In Cisco Local AP mode (default lightweight mode), every AP builds two CAPWAP tunnels to the WLC—one for management/control (UDP 5246) and one for centrally switching all client data frames (UDP 5247) (D). By contrast, FlexConnect supports local switching directly onto branch VLANs and survives WAN outages to the WLC in standalone mode.",
