      explanation: "An IPv6 Anycast address is a unicast-range address assigned to multiple interfaces/devices simultaneously so routers deliver each packet to the topologically nearest node (one-to-nearest). An IPv6 Multicast address (FF00::/8) provides one-to-many delivery to all group members and can never serve as a packet's source address.",
